WEBVTT

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.700
There it is, Hakumei.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.170
That's the border of Makinata.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.050
Wow, that's it!

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.010
We'll arrive before the day is done.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.130
You've always dreamed of seeing Makinata, right? What do you think?

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.390
I've only seen the gate, so I don't know!

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.600
When we get there, let's all grab drinks.
I'll buy a round for everyone!

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.940
Or at least, I'll owe you one until I work my way up in the caravan.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.860
Actually, I'm not sure that's gonna happen.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.240
Don't merchants in the caravan get promotions?

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.250
Well, Hakumei...

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.120
This is where we part.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.460
Be careful out there.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.010
Emerald Tail!

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.010
I want to stay with the caravan after all!

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.030
Hey.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.900
That looks heavy. What did you bring with you?

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.450
Homemade explosives.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.530
Explosives?

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:43.240
Y'know, in case there are any obstacles on the way.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.790
You'll blow them up?

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.580
We won't make it in time if we get stopped along the way.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.340
We just need to make it to Koyou Boulder by sunrise tomorrow, right?

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.220
I hope we'll be able to see Ol' Emerald Tail's caravan.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.800
If the newspaper's right, they're going south on their way back from a trading trip.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:06.480
It would be so much easier if they stopped by Makinata, though.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:12.320
The Pathfinder's Festival is tomorrow, as well.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.150
Konju was excited about singing on the new stage.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:23.490
The old tent turned into a tsukumogami at the last harvest festival, right?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.290
Anyway, it's just kind of unfortunate.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.170
There are size restrictions on entering Makinata.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:33.710
Ol' Emerald Tail is almost twice as large as the upper limit.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.050
Oh, right. I'd forgotten about that rule.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.350
Hakumei?

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.270
Right, let's hurry.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.860
Let's take the Hinochi highway first and head to Kaharu Bridge.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.360
When we cross the bridge, we'll ride the cable car to Koyou Boulder.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.030
If we can get on the cable car today,
we should make it in time.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.910
That's cutting it real close.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.120
But isn't the Hinochi highway...

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.340
It's an abandoned road, isn't it? I knew it.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.220
Yeah, they're not maintaining it.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.840
But some folks use it, even now.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.340
They do?

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.430
I'm... surprised... that anyone could use—

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.270
Watch your step.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.560
They use it <i>because</i> it's like this.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.150
Travelers who want to lay low,
and street racers and such.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.910
If we can get one of 'em to give us a ride, then we'd save a lot of time.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.990
I'm sure we would.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.660
Oh, look. There's one.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.000
What's this? A furball?

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.290
No idea, but I'm pretty sure it's an animal.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.590
Hey! How about taking the two of us to Koyou for five hundred?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.140
I ain't going all the way to Koyou.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.890
That five hundred could get you across Kaharu Bridge.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.190
That's a high price. What kind of speed are we getting for our money?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.780
Pay up first.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.450
Can't you go any faster?

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.290
Don't be stupid. You're gonna fall.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:40.590
Hey, Hakumei. Tell me more about the Emerald Tail Caravan.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.470
They helped you out when you were homeless, right?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.800
Yeah.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.520
It was organized by the merchants of Yashiro to be a trade caravan and peacekeeping force.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.850
Trading's their bread and butter,

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:00.900
but they're also top-rate intelligence and combat specialists.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.740
They do about five trade expeditions per year.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.580
Each journey can last from ten days to a month.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.920
When they're not trading,
they work as a vigilante police force.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:25.470
Even the infamous thieves of Yashiro
take time off when they're in town.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.010
Most feared among them is the leader, Ol' Emerald Tail.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:36.850
She's an elderly wolf in charge of everything the caravan does.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:42.150
One eye. Ashen-white fur. Age unknown.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.030
The tip of her tail is dyed a stylish green.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.420
A long time ago, when the caravan only numbered a few,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:03.130
they were carrying out a big deal involving jewels and alcohol.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:08.840
One day, a band of thieves that held a grudge tracked the caravan all the way from Yashiro.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.310
As they were heading back home,
on a moonless night,

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.940
the brigands set fire to the campgrounds.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.900
They planned to use the chaos and confusion to attack.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.490
However!

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.330
Their schemes had not gone unnoticed.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.590
How fortunate. I was just looking for some extra hands.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.800
Will you die here, or help carry our wares?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.630
The choice is yours.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.560
So one thing led to another,
and their membership swelled.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:00.190
By the time I'd met them, there were several dozen caravan subgroups.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.060
They're part of the lifeblood of the country now.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:08.240
Wow. Was it the main group that found you when you collapsed in the street?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.820
That's right.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:16.450
I'm surprised they went out of their way to bring you all the way to Makinata.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.790
Well, about that...

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.170
I did ask them the reason, once.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.460
What did they say? Tell me!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.050
Well, Ol' Emerald Tail...

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:32.130
She really liked my red hair.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.310
She said she'd like to keep it around as long as possible.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.350
Oh?

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.690
I felt uncomfortable taking them up on their offer, but I worked real hard to make up for it.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.190
You're going to meet up with those people?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:56.030
No, we won't be able to meet them,
but I wanted to get at least a glimpse.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.370
Oh, yeah?

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.710
I'll try and pick up the pace, then.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.830
Hey, thanks!

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.760
Hey, we've reached Kaharu Bridge.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.970
How long are you gonna lay there?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.390
I feel sick...

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.690
It looks like something's wrong, though.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.440
Everyone's gathered around.
Looks like they can't cross over.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.770
What?!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:32.280
As I've been saying, one part of the column has started to rot...

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.660
I'll fix it right up!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.700
Please don't be absurd.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.290
You'll have to find another way, I guess.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.170
But then we wouldn't make it in time.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.840
Well, I did promise to take you <i>across</i> the bridge...

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:03.390
Do you have anything to strap yourselves on with? I'll bring you over.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.820
Hey, can you really climb up the other side?!

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.990
No talking! You'll bite your tongue!

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.250
What's this rock doing here?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.250
What's wrong?

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.670
The path to the opposite shore is blocked.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:35.630
And there's no footing here to try'n push it over.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:40.220
What're we gonna do? This is the only route.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.220
Aren't you glad I brought them?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.730
Will that one explosive be enough?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.110
Probably, yeah.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:59.410
I'll let you know when I light the fuse, so be ready to bail.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.530
This is freaking scary.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.330
It's lit!

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.840
Now we can pass!

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.550
Amazing...

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.430
Why are you carrying something so dangerous?

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.230
For fun and profit!

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.570
All right, we're across.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.070
Wow!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.820
What'll you do now?

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.660
We'll take the cable car over to the boulder.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.700
The gondola? They'll be closing up soon, you know.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.290
Huh?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.330
This early?!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.000
What are we gonna do? Run for it?

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.630
About how far are we from there?

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.840
P-Pretty far is how far we are!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.300
Will we m-make it in time?!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.590
I-I-It's gonna be really hard to make it in time!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.680
We have to get going right aw—

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.110
The gondola's still there!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.520
Two adults!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.610
You can pay when you get there.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.200
Thank you! You've helped so much!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.620
Sure thing. I hope you can see your friends.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:32.920
The car's going to sway when you get going and when we change operators, okay?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.000
Okay.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.750
I'm glad we made it.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:39.510
This is my first time in a gondola.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.010
Off you go.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.220
Are you okay?

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.020
That hurt.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.940
Huh? Where'd the explosives go?

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.400
Wait! You're stepping on them!

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.530
I'm hungry.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.580
Wanna eat a late night snack?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.830
I've got a peanut!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:26.760
By the way, there was something today I wanted to ask.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.060
Hmm?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:34.310
Didn't you ever think to join the caravan
instead of staying behind at Makinata?

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:40.650
You could've visited all sorts of places.
Isn't that what you loved doing?

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:42.820
Yeah, well...

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.830
I did think about it, you know.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.870
I'd gotten pretty used to the caravan life.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.660
Well then, why did you stay in Makinata?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:57.580
I'd heard it was a weird country, so I wanted to visit.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.260
Plus, Ol' Emerald Tail stopped me from becoming a member.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.630
She did?

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.970
Well, Hakumei...

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.890
This is where we part.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:18.400
Be careful out there.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:24.650
You knew that there was a size limit all along?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.200
Yeah.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.740
Can't do anything about it.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.240
What a total letdown.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:38.670
I heard that Makinata was a strange place made up of travelers ready to settle down.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.000
I had high hopes for it.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:46.090
But I can't believe that they turn people away at the gate just because of how big they are.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.720
That's just...

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.680
despicable.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.180
Emerald Tail!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.270
I want to stay with the caravan after all!

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.610
You can't.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:09.780
We're going home to Yashiro. But you don't consider Yashiro your home, do you?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.240
So far, you've seen almost nothing of Makinata,

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.660
and you know almost nothing about its rules.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:22.250
It's precisely because you're capable of going anywhere that you ought to try living here.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.430
And, Hakumei...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:37.480
If you ever feel you want to leave, there will
always be a place in the caravan for you.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.400
My hair was super long at the time,

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.950
but I cut it right then and there
and gave it to Ol' Emerald Tail.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:53.200
I wanted to give her something to remember me by.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.210
Hey. Have you thought about growing it out again?

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.540
Nope. It gets in the way when it's long.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.230
What's happening?!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.350
You've arrived!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.530
We're here already?

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.070
Good morning.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.370
Here's some firewood for you to use.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.660
Thanks.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.500
You came to catch the sunrise, right?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.840
Take your time and enjoy the view.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.670
Thanks!

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:49.090
The sunrise, huh? That'll be a nice bonus!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.860
I can't see anything.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:10.990
It's maybe about one or two hours until dawn.

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:14.410
My limbs feel like lead, but my eyes are wide awake.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.780
Same here.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.300
Hey, Hakumei.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.300
Hm?

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:38.470
You've lived in Makinata for a while. How do you feel about it now?

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.060
That's a good question.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.560
I don't really know.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.320
But...

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.280
I think it's a place I can call home.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.420
Looks like the sun will be up soon.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.130
Yeah.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.380
Hold up! It's not this direction!

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:16.390
What isn't?

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.600
Look over there! This is the direction we came from!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.970
We were looking entirely the wrong way!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.770
Then does that mean they've...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.110
There they are!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.650
Huh?!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.380
Ol'... Ol' Emerald Tail!

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.380
I can only see her behind!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.510
They totally slipped by without me noticing.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:01.510
Hey! Everyone in the caravan!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:07.190
I'm doing fine over here!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.330
All right, ready to go home?

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.540
Already?!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:30.380
It's fine. I knew that my voice can't reach them from here, anyway.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.300
At least I got to see her face... Or her rear, anyway.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.670
I'm satisfied with that.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:39.840
Hakumei...

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.390
Didn't you have one more with you?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.600
One more thing that makes a <i>very</i> loud noise.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.990
Hey, Operator-san!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.610
What is it?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.990
I have a favor to ask you!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.410
So, throw this high up in the air, right?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.330
Yes.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.250
It's so small that it'll be hard to throw.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.920
Can I tie it to a stone or something?

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:15.960
Sure.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:20.380
Even though it's small, it's an explosive.
And the ground here is a bit unstable.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.600
Please throw it as high as you can!

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:29.850
You got it! These shoulders haven't been working the pulleys for nothing. Let me show you what they can do!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.230
Okay!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:35.610
Now!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:48.700
What was that?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.000
An attack?

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.500
I'll check it out!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:56.750
What is it?

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:02.010
All clear! They self-destructed.
You guys should take a look!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.390
Is that...

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.760
What the hell is she doing?

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.530
I'm glad she seems to be doing well.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:25.120
Hakumei. You kept your hair short, did you?

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.080
You gonna respond to her, Boss?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.540
Of course.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.900
Let's go home.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.270
Yes, let's.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.190
I'm looking forward to the festival.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:25.510
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:33.270
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:37.270
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:41.320
the stars twinkle and shine

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:45.780
After we take in an easy breath,

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:50.330
the banquet will begin!

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:53.790
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:57.540
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:01.460
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:06.260
It's itching to dance with us

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:10.260
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:14.220
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:19.520
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:22.650
At least, that's how we're feeling

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:34.040
The rustling of the beech leaves plays at my ears

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:41.670
And the fall-blooming Clematis sway in the night wind.

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:49.760
The fanfare of the harvest festival parade reaches me from far away

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:54.310
My cheeks gain just a bit of color

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:59.230
Oh, it almost feels as if I'm floating

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:04.270
Pear tarts and a lemon pie

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:07.990
And a generous helping of dried figs

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.910
I can feel myself bursting into a grin

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:16.790
The whole world seems so exciting

00:23:16.790 --> 00:23:20.670
What kind of coffee shall we have?

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:24.750
Would a cinnamon roast be stylish, perhaps?

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:30.050
I feel as if I could fly up into the sky

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:33.010
And we're not even done yet
